  entries:
  - id: graverobber
    title: The Grave Robber
    pages:
    - "Recovered Field Note, Provisional Designation:\n\u201CThe Grave Robber\u201D\nSource
      redacted\n\nA recurring human presence has been connected to the majority of
      grave disturbances. The individual is believed to be a local resident who acts
      as the primary point of contact for outsiders engaging in theft and desecration.
      His true identity remains unknown.\n\nHe does not work alone. His accomplices
      are frequently observed scouting the cemetery during off hours, testing sightlines
      and response times. These individuals retreat when illuminated and have been
      successfully deterred with sustained use of flashlights. Constant vigilance
      is required, as their activity is ongoing and deliberate."
    - 'Foreigners arrive with detailed knowledge of the cemetery layout, patrol patterns,
      and access routes, despite having no prior connection to the area. This information
      is presumed to be supplied by him. Activity increases sharply following his
      arrival and disperses once he leaves.


      The Grave Robber is violent.
      Evidence suggests intentional intimidation rather than necessity. Damaged tools,
      excessive force, and signs of internal conflict among accomplices indicate
      a leadership role maintained through fear.


      Previous gravekeepers have
      reported encounters. In each case, documentation ends shortly afterward. One
      keeper abandoned the post without notice. Another was hospitalized with injuries
      inconsistent with a fall. A third recorded a sighting but the final entry was
      torn from the log.'
    - He avoids identification. Facial details vary between reports, and no reliable
      image has been captured. Despite this, his presence is unmistakable. Continued
      observation is necessary. Direct confrontation is not advised.
  - id: yurei
    title: The Yurei
    pages:
    - "Recovered Field Note, Informal Designation:\n\u201CThe Yurei\u201D\n\nA new
      presence has been identified within the cemetery. The timing suggests a recent
      burial, though the associated grave has not been confirmed. Activity began
      abruptly, as if the role was assumed rather than developed over time.\n\nThe
      entity demonstrates heightened emotional sensitivity. Human presence produces
      variable effects that appear personal in nature. Some visitors report a sense
      of calm or hesitation, as though gently encouraged to remain. Others experience
      unease, intrusive thoughts, and a strong impression of being unwelcome."
    - 'Behavior indicates selective judgment. Entry is sometimes impeded without
      physical obstruction, while access is quietly permitted in other cases. These
      decisions do not appear consistent, suggesting internal conflict rather than
      intent to harm.


      Disrespect toward the grounds results in immediate
      mental disturbance among those responsible. The effect subsides once order
      is restored. No physical damage has been attributed directly to the entity.


      The
      Yurei appears bound to the cemetery and invested in its preservation. She seeks
      rest, yet remains vigilant. Her attachment to certain individuals complicates
      her function. Continued observation is necessary.'
  - id: wraith
    title: The Wraith
    pages:
    - "Recovered Field Note, Informal Designation:\n\u201CThe Wraith\u201D\nLocation
      withheld\n\nThe ledger bears its mark before I see a body.\n\nI have walked
      these grounds for years, and yet the air changes when it passes. It is not
      seen, not in the way one expects a creature to appear. Only the silence gives
      it away.\n\nThose it chooses do not flee. There is no chase. There is no struggle.
      By the time anyone notices, it has already claimed them. There is no mistaking
      it; this entity appears to be the most dangerous among the documented."
    - "It is drawn to strength. The capable, the defiant, the prepared, they are
      its prey. The weak may go unnoticed, but the strong... those it deems worthy,
      are ended with precision. No survivor can recount the encounter. Only the evidence
      remains, subtle and cruel.\n\nI do not know how it moves, or where it comes
      from. \nReports only conclude that encounters with this creature will not result
      in a conventional hunt."
  - id: friend
    title: The Friend
    pages:
    - "Recovered Field Note, Informal Designation:\n\u201CThe Friend\u201D\nStrange
      encounter\n\nToday I noticed unusual changes. Temperatures dropped suddenly
      without explanation. Small objects were found displaced as though something
      had passed through. Movements were slight, almost imperceptible, but persistent.\n\nThere
      is a sensation, difficult to describe, of being observed. Shadows appear heavier,
      and sometimes I feel a presence just beyond the edge of vision. It moves cautiously,
      avoiding direct light, and does not make sound unless provoked. The pattern
      is inconsistent, yet deliberate enough to suggest awareness."
    - 'I observed subtle traces that cannot be accounted for. Surfaces that were
      previously still show signs of disturbance. The air often feels dense afterward,
      as if retaining a memory of motion. The changes are not violent but are repeated
      with unnerving regularity.


      I recorded these anomalies carefully. There
      is no structural damage, no sign of interference by humans, and no explanation
      that fits the observations. Yet the events continue, and each instance leaves
      the same oppressive, lingering impression.


      I cannot explain it. Whatever
      it is, it does not appear fully aware of its actions, yet its presence affects
      the space profoundly. The true threat from this creature is felt from their
      absence. I will continue to note any further occurrences and record patterns
      as they emerge.'
  - id: beast
    title: The Beast
    pages:
    - "Recovered Field Note, Informal Designation: \n\u201CThe Beast\u201D\nSource
      redacted\n\nSurvivors agree on this much: the creature does not announce itself.
      It waits until it has judged you. Signs of weakness of mind appear to draw
      it closer. It watches for hesitation. For the moment your thoughts slow and
      your will folds inward.\n\nThose who never realize they were being hunted often
      report nothing at all. They vanish quietly. No screams or signs of pursuit.
      The Beast does not waste energy on panic."
    - 'When it does show itself, it is deliberate and brief. A silhouette where there
      should be none.


      It favors concealment over speed, patience over force.
      It will remain unseen for hours, sometimes days, tracking the same individual
      until the prey convinces it - through fear, isolation, or doubt, that the kill
      will be effortless.


      Those who stare at it lose their mind. It is also
      known to interfere with electronic equipment.'
  - id: bride
    title: The Bride
    pages:
    - "Recovered Field Note, Provisional Designation:\n\u201CThe Bride\u201D\nUnknown
      encounter\n\n"
    - This entry appears to be empty.
